[0.005, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'm reading the engine's departure, cruise and\u001b[50Gdocking-approach\u001b[67Gcode,\u001b[73Gso\u001b[76GI can prop\u001b[87Gse\u001b[90Ga lan\u001b[96G design\u001b[104Gbefore\u001b[111Gtouching\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Banything.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mSea\u001b[7Gching f\u001b[15Gr \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m pattern, re\u001b[31Gding \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m fil\u001b[42Gs, listing \u001b[1m1\u001b[55G\u001b[22mdirec\u001b[62Gry…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  ~/projects/manifest/source/game/travel/src/Travel.cpp\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B← \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Lane shape \u001b[39m\u001b[49m ☐ Lane choice \u001b[33G☐\u001b[35GScope\u001b[42G✔\u001b[44GSubmit\u001b[52G→\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mHow should opposite flows be kept apart along a cruise and at its ends?\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mKeep right (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEvery cruise is offset to the right of its direction of travel (right taken against the system's up), from its \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mdeparture gate to its arrival gate. A→B and B→A become parallel lines a few km apart for the whole trip. At each \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mstation, departures to B and arrivals from B sit side by side on the side facing B. This works like road traffic \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Band Freelancer's paired one-way lanes, and the offset changes smoothly with direction.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[39m Levels\u001b[13Gby heading\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mAviation'\u001b[16G sem\u001b[21Gcircular rule: cruises heading one half of the compass fly above the orbit plane and the other half \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bbelow it, so opposite headings never share a level. Proven in aviation, but the flip at the boundary heading means \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mtwo nearly parallel cruises ca\u001b[37G be on different levels. Departures climb and arrivals descend to their level.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3. Type something.\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  4.\u001b[6GChat\u001b[11Gabout\u001b[17Gthis\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0014 ─\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[13;1H"]
