m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Measured on today's engine, six starters flown both ways between Highport and Vale never came within 198 m of \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Beach other, hull to hull, checked between steps too. Courses flown both ways in the same hour are about 5,400 km \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bapart, because each aims where its target will be and the stations move about 15° an hour. What is shared: ships \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bgoing the same way fly the same line 6–70 m apart, kept apart only by leaving seconds after one another, and a \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bdeparture passes about 800 m from an arrival. Highport's four pads also cap how many leave at once. How should we \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mproce\u001b[12Gd?\u001b[15G→ Keep test, park lanes (Recommended)\r\u001b[17C\u001b[8B (shift+tab to cycle) · esc to interrupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
