[0.030, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3\u001b[6G\u001b[1mOrbits in\u001b[16Gthe \u001b[21Gample.\u001b[22m For the reference frames to stay byte-identical, the sample needs its\u001b[98Gown copy of the\u001b[114Gorbit\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bm\u001b[8Gths\u001b[12G(abou\u001b[18G 150 lines).\u001b[31GThe\u001b[35Galternativ\u001b[46G is sim\u001b[55Ge circular orbits, with\u001b[79Gevery\u001b[85Greference\u001b[95Gframe\u001b[101Gre-made\u001b[109Gonce.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe estimate of\u001b[19Gthe\u001b[23Gsample's share is rough, and I haven't yet\u001b[66Gchecked\u001b[74Ghow much Mani\u001b[89Gst's content loading depends\u001b[118Gon\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcelestial\u001b[39m's\u001b[15Gdefinition\u001b[26Gtypes.\u001b[33GThis\u001b[38Gis\u001b[41Ga\u001b[43Ggood\u001b[48Gpoint\u001b[54Gfor\u001b[58Ga\u001b[60Gfresh\u001b[66Gsession;\u001b[75GI'd\u001b[79Grun\u001b[83Gslice\u001b[89G1\u001b[91Gonward\u001b[98Gon\u001b[101GOpus\u001b[106Gat\u001b[109Ghigh\u001b[114Geffort.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCooked for 2m 47s · done 7:03 pm\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mJettison's space sample has served it's purpose well. Manifest is now available to test all space game related code. \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mManifest is where future work will build towards a fully featured game that is able to be modded by players.\u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mYou may fold the small test samp\u001b[36Ge\u001b[38Ginto o\u001b[45Gher text\u001b[55Gixtures if that is\u001b[74Gsui\u001b[78Gable and\u001b[87Greduce the amount of surface area\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexposed. Keep it if it still provides high value test e.g. frame captures, or testing that is not possible or \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bavail\u001b[9Gble elsewhere.\u001b[39m                                                                                                 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────── 1 new message ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m That's a bigger simplification. I'll revise the plan to retire the space sample: Manifest tests all space code, and\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bonly\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Gsample's\u001b[21Guniquely\u001b[30Gvaluable\u001b[39Gtests\u001b[45Gstay,\u001b[51Gfolded\u001b[58Ginto\u001b[63Gneutral\u001b[71Gfixtures.\u001b[81GFirst,\u001b[88Gan\u001b[91Gaudit\u001b[97Gof\u001b[100Gwhat\u001b[105Gthe\u001b[109Gsample's\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gtes\u001b[7Gs and the smoke and frame runs actually\u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
