[0.169, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[2m8\u001b[12G\u001b[22m  \u001b[15Goptional list. Manifest's \u001b[42Guites and pins hel\u001b[62Gon the new SDK pin.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 129 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m7. **Close-out.** The allow-list empty; architecture, scope, game integration and the sample docs     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 129 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m7. **Saved names.** Every saved and reflected name still in the setting's words or the old module's   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 130 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   (`\"byHull\"`, `Ai.OnLane`, `Ai.Cruising` and the rest) renamed at once: one save version and its    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 131 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   rename table, so a save written before loads, and every pin moved once, shown to be the names      \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m32\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  \u001b[15Galone by each hash returning\u001b[44Gwith the old names\u001b[63Gput back. B\u001b[75Gfore players keep saves\u001b[100Gr write    \r\u001b[8C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m3\u001b[15G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mmods against\u001b[28Gthe names (the use\u001b[47G's, 2026-11-22).     \u001b[69G       \u001b[77G  \u001b[80G     \u001b[86G   \u001b[90G    \u001b[95G       \u001b[103G   \u001b[107G   \r\u001b[8C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m4\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m8.\u001b[15G**Close-out.** The\u001b[34Gallow-l\u001b[42Gs\u001b[44G empty; architecture, scope, ga\u001b[76Ge integration a\u001b[92Gd the sample docs\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 135 \u001b[22m    rewritten for the boundary as it is; Manifest's boundary assessment's status; the consumer matrix\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 136 \u001b[22m    (ground, Manifest) run; a cross-review of the whole, as at a stage's end.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 137 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\