[0.004, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ cd '/home/ivan/projects/jettison'/../manifest && git grep -n -i -E 'kPinned|pinned|StateHash\\(\\) \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m==|0x[0-9a-f]{16}' -- source | grep -v '^source/.*\\.md' | wc -l; git grep -l -E '0x[0-9a-f]{16}' -- source | head; \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mgit grep -n -B3 -A12 'Dock::Carry' -- source/game/travel/tests/TravelTests.cpp | head…\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Cargo deck \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mRemoving the cargo deck moves pinned world hashes: a save writes every registered component's name, so dropping \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mDock.Transfer and Dock.Buggy changes the bytes of every Manifest and Jettison pin with docks attached. Manifest also \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mloads `bays:`/`traffic:` in Ore Highport's layout and uses Dock::Carry in one travel test, to get a departure refused.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mHow should slice 2 handle it?\r\u001b[2B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mKeep two names\u001b[21G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRecommended. Delete the deck's code, layout fields, reason and tests now. Keep Dock.Transfer and Dock.Buggy \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mregistered, with no behaviour,\u001b[37Guntil slice 7 renames and drops saved names in one pin move. Pins hold now. Manifest\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bdrops bays/traffic from its data and finds another way to get a departure refused.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[39m Move\u001b[11Gpins now\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mDelete everythi\u001b[22Gg n\u001b[26Gw, including the two regi\u001b[53Grations. Every pin\u001b[72Gmoves twice: now, shown to be those two names \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Balone, and again in slice 7.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mDefer to slice 7\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mLeave the deck in place now. Slice 5 then has to carry it when it converts the dock to berths, against the plan's \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mdelete-before-converting\u001b[31Grul\u001b[35G.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m4. Type something.\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  5.\u001b[6GChat\u001b[11Gabout\u001b[17Gthis\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · ↑/↓ to navigate · Esc to cancel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0014 ─\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[12;1H"]
